{%- comment -%}
  NF-SEARCH-HEAD v3 (2026-10-24, owner: "make it look like MOD"): Back, "Results for “term”" with the count, one line.
  The old centered header (gold eyebrow, huge quoted term, "Found in" collection chips) is gone. Styles: nf-m6.css P.
  Params: terms, count, items (kept for callers; items is no longer used).
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'nf-search.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<div class="nf-srch-head nfsr">
  <a class="nfsr__back" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" onclick="if (history.length > 1 && document.referrer.indexOf(location.host) > -1) { history.back(); return false; }"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="12" height="12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 8H3.5M7.5 4L3.5 8l4 4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Back</a>
  <h1 class="nfsr__h">Results for &ldquo;{{ terms | escape }}&rdquo; <span class="nfsr__n">({{ count }})</span></h1>
  <p class="nfsr__sub">Every light, guide and idea matching your search.</p>
</div>
